From feb65e2cd74fbf3e264b2b4e30341a8004a4fc9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olympia <olympia@xbmc.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:28:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Fix lost and stale change flags of the information
 dialog

[Video] Reset the updated items flag of the information dialog (e03d83c)

The flag telling the caller that versions or extras were changed was
never reset, so after managing them once every later information dialog
refreshed the whole list, even when nothing changed. It is now reset
when the dialog opens, and kept when the dialog opens itself again for
another item or after a cancelled play. Managing versions or extras a
second time without a change no longer clears it either.

[Video] Do not skip a requested refresh after a user rating change (6807623)

After the information dialog closed, the video window checked for a
changed user rating before it checked whether Refresh was pressed. A
rating change followed by Refresh therefore only reloaded the list, and
the item was never refreshed. The changes made in the dialog are now
checked after that, and are still reported when the requested refresh
fails, is cancelled or cannot run.

[Video] Keep the change flags when the information dialog reopens (ef07d4a)

The information dialog opens itself again when it moves on to another
item, or after a cancelled play. Opening resets the flags telling the
caller that art or the user rating was changed, so a change made before
was lost and the list was not refreshed. They are now kept across these
openings, as the updated items flag already is.

[Video] Save the user rating before the information dialog moves on (ea1593d)

The user rating set in the information dialog was only written to the
database when the dialog closed, compared with the rating of the item it
shows by then. Moving on to another movie through the cast or a movie set
replaces that item first, so the changed rating was never saved, while
the list already showed it. The rating is now saved before the dialog
moves on.

[Video] Report art changes of every art type chosen in a row (4b5aa9d)

Choosing art goes through the art types in a loop, and only the result
of the last type opened was returned. Saving a poster and then backing
out of the fanart browser reported no change, so the information dialog
and the Manage menu did not refresh the list for the saved poster. Any
art saved in the loop is now reported.

Backported to Kodi 21.3-Omega (a3a448d) for the OSMC vero5 build from
xbmc/xbmc#30138 (4b5aa9d), its five commits squashed. In Omega
CVideoInfoTag has no GetMediaType(), so the media type is read from
m_type and compared to MediaTypeVideoCollection.

Omega's CGUIWindowVideoBase::ShowInfo() returns a bool, true when the
list has to be updated, and has no ShowInfoResult. Where upstream
returns RESULT_ERROR it now returns whether the dialog made changes,
which also covers Omega's return when there is no scraper. A rating
change no longer returns early, as upstream.

Omega's CArtTypeChooser has no UpdateArtType(), so in
ChooseAndManageVideoItemArtwork() only the result is fixed.
